From 4de65bc6c88b97607f22311cb02ae9ab7100e294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:44:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] proprietary-files: drop 1,875 blobs nothing on this tablet
 uses

From a reachability audit of the vendor partition (port vendor/blob-audit.md):
camera tuning, sensor, actuator and EEPROM libraries of other Huawei
devices' sensors (camera_config_Agassi.xml names the four this tablet can
have), mobile network/IMS/RCS and data-path code, Huawei factory and MMI
test code, clients of unused TrustZone apps, stock-kernel modules and
libraries that cannot link on Android 10. None is loaded, linked or named
by anything that stays; parked on the tablet, boot and features unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 proprietary-files.txt | 1875 -----------------------------------------
 1 file changed, 1875 deletions(-)

